      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-i/q8-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"up the plane: [A1] 3g −T = 3a, T + 7g sin θ −3.36g = 7a. [A1] The reaction is 7g(4/5) = 5.6g; friction is 0.6(5.6g) = 3.36g. Adding the two signed equations cancels T, leaving 3g + 4.2g −3.36g = 10a. Adding gives 10a = 3.84g, [A1] hence a = 3.7632 m s−2 . [A1] The first equation gives T = 3g −3(3.7632) ≈18.11 N . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
